From b211c9d3eab1310eda2e511c965da3cf5910290e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 09:09:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] drm, rendervulkan: apply final review findings

- Never combine an explicit modifier list with GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR:
  GBM rejects that with EINVAL (Mesa gbm.c), so linear requests now
  allocate directly with gbm_bo_create and report DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR.
- Destroy m_lumaView/m_chromaView in ReleaseResources; previously two
  VkImageViews leaked per destroyed YCbCr texture.
- Probe only DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR for linear flippable textures
  (cursor) instead of Vulkan-validating every KMS modifier and
  discarding the results.
- Only request an output-image rebuild when the drm_gbm_scanout value
  actually changes; ConVar callbacks also run for writes of the
  unchanged value.
- Deduplicate the modifier-probe construction into
  BSupportsExternalScanoutModifier() and share the usage derivation
  between BInitInternal and the probes via VulkanUsageFromCreateFlags(),
  so the external-scanout intersection cannot diverge from the image
  BInitInternal actually creates.
- Trim the drm_gbm_scanout description to codebase style and reword
  comments to state invariants rather than describe the change.

